# Endpoint that receives lead submissions (Contact, Request a Quote, Support
# forms). Point this at your own backend/serverless function or email
# service (e.g. an AWS Lambda, a Formspree-style endpoint, etc).
#
# If left unset, forms fall back to a simulated submission so the UI can
# still be reviewed end-to-end without a backend connected.
VITE_LEAD_API_URL=

# Never put real API keys or credentials in this file if it will be
# committed — only the public, non-secret values belong on the frontend.
# Secret keys (email provider keys, database credentials, etc.) must live
# on the backend/serverless function that VITE_LEAD_API_URL points to.

# Endpoint for the AI Agent chat widget (bottom-right of every page).
# Expected contract: POST { message, history } -> { reply, quickReplies?, link? }
#
# If left unset, the widget answers from the site's own services/industries/
# FAQ data using local keyword matching — no key or backend required.
#
# To upgrade to a real LLM (e.g. Claude), point this at a small backend or
# serverless function that calls the Anthropic API server-side. The
# Anthropic API key must live in that backend's environment, never here —
# anything in a VITE_ variable is bundled into the public frontend code.
VITE_CHAT_API_URL=
